  Why: 'Walls 023-039 (LedgeCliff) stand on a bench at -1.65. In front of it the plan lays a reef: a toe channel the walls'' foot keeps, then a weed-covered crest that bares at every low, cut by gullies along the rock''s joints and pocked with rock pools. Its walls (PR 5w, by real id, clockwise): 023, 024, 025, 026, 027, 028, 147, 148, 149, 029, 030, 150, 031, 151, 032, 152, 153, 154, 033, 155, 156, 034, 157, 035, 158, 036, 159, 160, 161, 162, 163, 164, 165, 037, 038, 166, 039; part 2 drew it on walls 023-039. (terrain pass 9 part 2, p2_data.py sha256 15750c11...; PR 5w, on the ground file: paint only)'
